{
  "_comment": "Mako infusions (owner design 2026-11-09; one effect each, owner 2026-11-10). From round 1 on, the battle pauses on the game's own message window offering per_offer random infusions; the pick lasts the rest of the run and a taken infusion is never offered again. Each has exactly one effect: 'statuses' (one BattleStatusChange row; 'time': 'short' makes it a brief opener each round instead of lasting the battle), 'special' (a BattleSpecialStatusChange row, given again whenever it lapses; 'each_round': true gives it once per round only; with 'seconds' beside it, it is given again whenever it lapses until that many fight seconds into the round, then left to lapse: owner 2026-11-11, Turbulent Spirit for 60 s, three of its natural 20 s), or 'action' (atb_full, limit_full or limit_level at the start of each round; heal_on_kill whenever an enemy falls; limit_over_time is Gotterdammerung's effect, which buffwheel.lua approximates while a round runs; limit_full and limit_over_time are no longer offered since owner 2026-11-11 but the code stays), or 'accessory' (an Equipment row such as E_ACC_0211: the native helper gives the party that real accessory's skill effects and ailment immunities without equipping it; offered only while the helper answers ready; materia accessories and immunities count from the next round; with 'materia' beside it, the accessory is a carrier row this mod adds to the Equipment table, a clone of HP Up Materia Earrings naming that materia, for the stat-up materia the game has no earrings for: tools/apply_buff_wheel.py, owner 2026-11-11). Tiers (owner 2026-11-10): each option of an offer first draws a tier by tier_weights (only tiers with an infusion left count), then one infusion of that tier at random, never one twice in an offer. The offer in the round after a boss round (course-design.json 'bosses') uses after_boss_weights, so epics are much more likely there. Common: the plain party wards (Protect, Shell, Regen, Resist) and the enemy ailments that wear a fight down (Slow, Weaken, Hex, Armor and Spell break, Silence). Rare: what changes a fight's tempo or damage (Haste, Brave, Faith, Reflect, Critical, Toxic, Turbulent Spirit (ATB regeneration), Full ATB, the Stop and Sleep openers, Reclaimant Choker, Mana surge, Enhanced Expeditionary Medal (limit level), and the ATB- and MP-fed limit gauges of Transference Module and Spectral Cogwheel). Accessory infusions follow the same scale: common for small passives and single immunities, rare for damage trades, status-duration accessories and materia earrings, epic for Genji Gloves, Ribbon and the Revival and Time materia. Labels stay within 48 characters with the tier prefix (the window is narrow). Owner 2026-11-11: an infusion that gives the party an accessory's effect says 'Party equips <the accessory's in-game name>' (materia earrings keep 'Gain the X ability' / 'Gain spells: ...'); Barret's ATB regeneration is 'Party gains Turbulent Spirit'; Assess is not offered. Epic: the run-defining ones (Reraise, Refocus and Gotterdammerung, the real accessory since owner 2026-11-11 in place of the full-limit-each-round and limit-over-time actions). tier_labels prefix the option text; commons have none. Labels may use Latin-1 letters (Götterdämmerung, as the game's own UI spells it). Generates Scripts/buffwheel_data.lua. Owner 2026-11-10: items can't be used in the colosseum, so item-only effects (Item Master) are not offered.",
